abstract @beta Efl.Object_Override
{
   [[The class an overriding function passes to efl_super() to reach the
     function it replaced.

     efl_object_override() gives one object functions of its own, from an
     array made with EFL_OPS_DEFINE(). Such a function calls the original
     implementation -- the one the object's class provides -- with
     $[efl_super(obj, EFL_OBJECT_OVERRIDE_CLASS)]:

     $[static int _my_value_get(const Eo *obj, void *pd)
     {
        return 1 + my_value_get(efl_super(obj, EFL_OBJECT_OVERRIDE_CLASS));
     }]

     It has no methods and no data, and is never instantiated or inherited
     from: it only names the step between an object's own functions and its
     class's.
   ]]
    data: null;
}
